	(property "Description" "JXTCONN CSIM-H137-7P-class nano-SIM push-push socket, 7 pads (5 ISO7816 SIM signal contacts VCC/RST/CLK/GND/IO + 2-pin mechanical card-detect switch CD1/CD2), H=1.37mm. Authored Task 14. DISCLOSED ASSUMPTION: JXTCONN's own pin-numbered mechanical drawing could not be retrieved (LCSC C42420236 product/EasyEDA API, JLCPCB SHOUHAN/hanxia clone listings, and prior gct.co/bsc-elec attempts all failed or returned no usable dimensioned drawing -- see task-11-report.md and this task's notes). Pad grid instead follows the REAL, successfully retrieved manufacturer drawing for ATTEND 115U-A103 ('Nano SIM Socket, 6 Pin Push Push, 1.4H, G/F, Reel', https://www.attend.com.tw/en/data/download/file/115U-A103_B_2.pdf): 1.27mm-pitch signal contact row (ATTEND's unused Vpp/C6 position omitted to match this part's 5-signal '7P' pinout), 0.80x1.14mm contact pads, a CD switch pad offset 0.95mm beyond the last signal contact (matching ATTEND's C5-to-CD offset), and a second switch/shell-ground pad (0.70x2.10mm) offset 1.67mm beyond the first signal contact (matching ATTEND's C3-to-GND-tab offset). This is a cross-vendor substitution, NOT JXTCONN's own drawing -- the pitch/size/offsets are a well-documented commodity nano-SIM push-push pattern, not confirmed against a JXTCONN or physical CSIM-H137-7P sample, and the outer body/silkscreen outline is an approximate envelope, not a traced JXTCONN body. NEEDS PHYSICAL-SAMPLE OR GENUINE-JXTCONN-DRAWING CONFIRMATION before layout lock. SEPARATE FLAG: ATTEND's own CARD DETECT SWITCH table shows the switch OPEN with no card and CLOSED with card inserted -- the opposite sense of a 'grounded=absent' convention -- cross-check against this project's DET polarity assumption (verification.md Item 7) before relying on CD1/CD2 sense in firmware; this is an electrical/schematic concern, not a footprint geometry concern."
		(at 0 0 0)
